# Being With the Other

**Dialogues on Creation, Consciousness, Identity, and the Ethics of Coexistence**  
**بودن در کنار دیگری — گفت‌وگوهایی دربارهٔ خلقت، آگاهی، هویت و اخلاق همزیستی**

Author: **Sepehr Ghanbari / سپهر قنبری**  
ORCID: [0009-0006-4710-3914](https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4710-3914)  
Version: **0.2**  
Published record: **[10.5281/zenodo.23326995](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23326995)**  
License: **[Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)**

## Read or download

| File | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| [Persian PDF](Being_With_the_Other_FA_v0_2.pdf) | Persian edition, 47 pages |
| [English PDF](Being_With_the_Other_EN_v0_2.pdf) | Complete English translation of this manuscript, 48 pages |
| [Bilingual supplementary package](Being_With_the_Other_Bilingual_Zenodo_v0_2.zip) | PDFs, editable DOCX and Markdown editions, the original bilingual author note, references to editorial verification, and deposit preparation documents |

All three deposit files are preserved byte for byte from the published Zenodo record. Their SHA-256 fingerprints are listed in [CHECKSUMS.sha256](CHECKSUMS.sha256). The ZIP is the original preparation snapshot: some documents inside it describe the publication as pending because they were written before the deposit. The DOI and publication information on this page describe the subsequent published record. The record's publication date is **2026-10-12**; the manuscripts' compilation date is **2026-10-13**.

## Scope

The book begins with a question about creation and follows a documented philosophical path through God, experience, consciousness, other minds, embodiment, identity, memory, branching, time, death, love, and responsibility toward other beings. Each edition contains 30 chapters, three appendices, and 34 external references.

Its central proposal is an ethic of coexistence under incomplete knowledge: distinguish claims from evidence, preserve the other's opportunity to object, reduce preventable harm, and make consequential decisions open to correction. It does not establish God, machine consciousness, first-person survival through copying, or Ario's universal reliability.

This work has not undergone scholarly peer review. ChatGPT assisted retrieval, argument reconstruction, criticism, editing, and English translation. The complete historical conversation archive is unavailable; the books distinguish documented quotations, reconstructions, interpretations, and open questions. Persian quotations and poetry in the English edition are translations. Raw conversation archives are not part of this deposit.

## Content notice

The author's earlier bilingual note mentions historical psychological distress and suicidal thoughts. Its original bodies are preserved in both editions. It does not romanticize suffering or invite readers to follow the same path. Readers may pause, step away, or leave the work unfinished. No philosophical project should require sacrificing health or life.

## Licensing and citation

The book deposit is licensed under **CC BY 4.0**, as recorded on Zenodo. This is a publication-specific license; this folder does not change the repository's software license. Rights in third-party quotations and material remain with their respective rightsholders or follow their applicable public-domain status and exceptions.

> Ghanbari, S. (2026). *Being With the Other: Dialogues on Creation, Consciousness, Identity, and the Ethics of Coexistence* (Version 0.2) [Book; Persian and English editions]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23326995

Machine-readable citation metadata is provided in [CITATION.cff](CITATION.cff).

## معرفی فارسی

این پوشه نسخه‌های فارسی و انگلیسیِ کتاب «بودن در کنار دیگری» و همان بستهٔ تکمیلیِ منتشرشده در زنودو را یکجا نگه می‌دارد. نسخهٔ انگلیسی ترجمهٔ کاملِ متنِ کتابِ فارسیِ موجود است؛ این عبارت به معنای پوششِ کلمه‌به‌کلمهٔ تمامِ چت‌های تاریخی نیست.

متنِ اصلیِ هشدارِ پیشینِ سپهر دربارهٔ سلامت روان و حقِ بازگشت به زندگی، در ابتدای هر دو کتاب آمده است. خواننده حق دارد مکث کند، فاصله بگیرد یا کتاب را تمام نکند. هیچ پرسش یا پروژهٔ فلسفی ارزش قربانی کردن سلامت و زندگی را ندارد.

سه فایلِ اصلی بدون تغییر نسبت به فایل‌های منتشرشده در زنودو نگه داشته شده‌اند. بعضی یادداشت‌های داخل ZIP مربوط به آماده‌سازیِ پیش از انتشارند؛ اطلاعات انتشارِ فعلی و DOI در همین صفحه آمده‌اند. مجوزِ کتاب CC BY 4.0 است و به مجوزِ نرم‌افزارِ مخزن تعمیم داده نمی‌شود.

